South Korean web browser
Naver Whale네이버 웨일Whale browser on Windows 11, WikipediaDeveloperNaver CorporationReleaseOctober 16, 2017; 8 years ago (2017-10-16)Stable release(s)macOS, Windows4.38.386.14[1]  / 25 June 2026Android3.9.14[2]  / 24 June 2026iOS, iPadOS3.9.16[3]  / 23 June 2026
EnginesBlink (WebKit on iOS/iPadOS), V8Operating systemAndroid 8.0 and lateriOS 15 and lateriPadOS 15 and latermacOS 10.15 and laterLinuxWindows 7 and laterPlatformIA-32, x86-64TypeWeb browser, mobile browserLicenseFreewareWebsitewhale.naver.com/en
Naver Whale (Korean: 네이버 웨일) is a freeware web browser developed by South Korean technology company Naver Corporation, which is available in English and Korean. It became available on Android on April 13, 2018.[4]
Naver Whale became available on Android on April 13, 2018.[5] Pages can be translated through its Naver Papago service and can translate from many other languages.[5] The Naver Whale browser has its own extensions that can be accessed through the Whale Store.[6]
Naver Whale Browser offers the ability called Whale On to conduct video conferencing without worrying about time limits.[7] Up to 500 people can access at the same time, and various functions such as screen sharing and microphone/camera control are available.[8]
